After the standalone GPIO peripheral is complete, it will be integrated with the existing Wishbone bus.

The resulting architecture will be:

                         CPU
                          │
                          ▼
                   Wishbone Bus
                          │
                  Address Decoder
                          │
          ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐
          ▼               ▼               ▼
         RAM             GPIO            UART
      0x0000            0x1000          0x2000
                          │
                          ▼
                       GPIO[7:0]

The goal is to make the GPIO accessible through a memory address in the same way that RAM and the existing UART will eventually be accessed.

This will complete the basic foundation for Memory-Mapped I/O.
